==Acquisition==
*This mod can be acquired by attaining the rank of '''Whirlwind''' under the [[Conclave]] [[Syndicate]], and spending {{sc|15,000}} to purchase.
*This mod can be obtained as a drop from [[Battalyst]]s.

==Drop Locations==
{{DropLocations}}

==Notes==
*Cannot be equipped on [[Sniper Rifle]]s or [[Bow]]s/crossbows
*Cannot be equipped on most primary weapons with the hidden <code>AOE</code> [[Compatibility Tag]]. The following weapons cannot equip the mod:
{{Column|2|
::*{{Weapon|Acceltra}} ({{Weapon|Acceltra Prime|Prime}})
::*{{Weapon|Aeolak}}
::*{{Weapon|Amprex}}
::*{{Weapon|Alternox}}
::*{{Weapon|Basmu}}
::*{{Weapon|Ignis}} ({{Weapon|Ignis Wraith|Wraith}})
::*{{Weapon|Javlok}}
::*{{Weapon|Kuva Chakkhurr}}
::*{{Weapon|Miter}}
::*{{Weapon|Ogris}} ({{Weapon|Kuva Ogris|Kuva}})
::*{{Weapon|Opticor}} ({{Weapon|Opticor Vandal|Vandal}})
::*{{Weapon|Penta}} (({{Weapon|Carmine Penta|Carmine}}), {{Weapon|Secura Penta|Secura}})
::*{{Weapon|Shedu}}
::*{{Weapon|Simulor}} ({{Weapon|Synoid Simulor|Synoid}})
::*{{Weapon|Stahlta}}
::*{{Weapon|Tenet Envoy}}
::*{{Weapon|Tonkor}} ({{Weapon|Kuva Tonkor|Kuva}})
::*{{Weapon|Torid}}
::*{{Weapon|Trumna}}
::*{{Weapon|Zarr}} ({{Weapon|Kuva Zarr|Kuva}})
}}
*The following weapons can equip the mod despite possessing an AoE component:
{{Column|1|
::*{{Weapon|Afentis}}
::*{{Weapon|Ambassador}}
::*{{Weapon|Battacor}}
::*{{Weapon|Ferrox}} ({{Weapon|Tenet Ferrox|Tenet}})
::*{{Weapon|Mutalist Quanta}})
::*{{Weapon|Panthera Prime}}
::*{{Weapon|Quanta}} ({{Weapon|Quanta Vandal|Vandal}})
::*{{Weapon|Scourge}} ({{Weapon|Scourge Prime|Prime}})
::*{{Weapon|Tenet Tetra}}
}}
*This mod reloads a portion of your weapon's magazine every second. It will not replenish a weapon's total ammo pool, and will partially reload the magazine if there is less than a full mag of ammo in the weapon's total pool.
*This mod will take effect when using quick melee, as this counts as holstering the weapon. A great strategy is to quick melee when your magazine gets low and do a few parkour moves to avoid enemies. By the time you finish, a large amount of your clip will be reloaded.
*This mod can be equipped to [[Speargun]]s to further enhance their innate ability to reload the magazine while holstered, boosting the total to 53%.
*Bonus stacks additively with the [[Set Mods#Synth Mod Set|Synth mod set bonus]].
*Weapons with a large magazine size, such as Quellor, can benefit greatly from this mod, especially if they have a long reload time.

